1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,725
Getting started with Neurodesk.

2
00:00:01,725 --> 00:00:08,193
Choose Play, EDU, or an institutional environment and verify that F S L is available.

3
00:00:08,193 --> 00:00:12,505
The goal is clear: Choose an appropriate Neurodesk access route.

4
00:00:13,355 --> 00:00:15,234
A reproducible software environment.

5
00:00:15,234 --> 00:00:18,521
Neurodesk packages neuroimaging applications in consistent environments.

6
00:00:18,521 --> 00:00:30,262
Neurodesk Play is broadly accessible; Neurodesk EDU may be provided by a course or institution; a local installation is optional and has higher hardware requirements.

7
00:00:30,262 --> 00:00:34,489
Files saved only inside temporary browser sessions may disappear.

8
00:00:34,489 --> 00:00:38,716
Use the persistent storage location provided by your environment.

9
00:00:38,716 --> 00:00:49,987
The base terminal is useful for general Linux work; an F S L terminal starts with the F S L software environment already loaded.

10
00:00:50,837 --> 00:00:54,167
Now connect the idea to an observable check.

11
00:00:54,167 --> 00:00:57,913
First, launch Neurodesk Play, EDU, or your institution's environment.

12
00:00:57,913 --> 00:01:00,827
Next, open the F S L application.

13
00:01:00,827 --> 00:01:07,070
Then, open its terminal and verify F S L with which F S L info.

14
00:01:07,070 --> 00:01:11,649
After that, identify the location where your files persist between sessions.

15
00:01:11,649 --> 00:01:14,979
The command shown on screen is an example.

16
00:01:14,979 --> 00:01:21,222
Adapt its path to your own working directory and verify the target before running it.

17
00:01:22,072 --> 00:01:24,072
F S L command not found?

18
00:01:24,072 --> 00:01:29,073
You may be in the base terminal rather than the F S L application terminal.

19
00:01:29,073 --> 00:01:35,075
Open the F S L tile, or load the F S L module if your environment supports modules.

20
00:01:35,075 --> 00:01:41,743
A useful self-check is this: What is the operational difference between the base terminal and an F S L terminal?

21
00:01:41,743 --> 00:01:52,411
The F S L terminal has the F S L environment loaded; the base terminal is a general shell and may not find F S L commands until a module is loaded.

22
00:01:53,261 --> 00:01:57,628
To recap: First, know which terminal you are using.

23
00:01:57,628 --> 00:02:00,539
Next, save work in persistent storage.

24
00:02:00,539 --> 00:02:04,420
Then, verify tools before starting a long analysis.

25
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:11,698
Before continuing, make sure you can explain this objective: Choose an appropriate Neurodesk access route.
